# [PROCON](../wg/procon.html)

## Summary

The PROCON working group met to review progress on its four active working group documents: draft-ietf-procon-2026bis, draft-ietf-procon-2418bis, draft-ietf-procon-chair-delegate, and draft-ietf-procon-chair-standin. 

Key outcomes included finalizing textual changes for draft-ietf-procon-2026bis and draft-ietf-procon-2418bis ahead of an upcoming joint Working Group Last Call (WGLC), as well as refining the delegation and stand-in models for the IETF Chair in draft-ietf-procon-chair-delegate and draft-ietf-procon-chair-standin.

## Key Discussion Points

### Administration and WG Status
- Working group chairs Jari Arkko and Leslie Daigle opened the session and presented the [Chair slides](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-procon-chair-slides-00).
- The chairs highlighted the recent minor charter update clarifying that PROCON outcome documents must accurately reflect current IETF operational practice. Actual changes to the process remain out of scope unless explicitly allowed by the charter (such as chair delegation and stand-in procedures).

### draft-ietf-procon-2026bis
Rich Salz presented updates using the [2026bis update](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-procon-2026bis-update-01) slide deck.
- **Draft-12 Changes:**
  - Clarified Last Call sequence text.
  - Replaced the sample reference (Ethernet instead of Unicode, suggested by John Klensin).
  - Avoided external links where possible (suggested by Jean Mahoney).
  - Explicitly stated that decisions are public, while conversations may be private and offline.
  - Added text allowing ADs to delegate handling of appeals/conflicts to another AD.
  - Clarified that the IESG determines IETF consensus.
  - Changed multi-month timeframes to fixed 60-day periods (noted by Sean Turner).
- **Open Issues and Planned Changes for Draft-13:**
  - **Draft Archival Text:** Removing outdated text stating that Internet-Drafts are deleted upon RFC publication.
  - **Terminology Harmonization:** Discussion on terms "conflict", "dispute", "complaint", and "appeal". Rich Salz, Barry Leiba, Jean Mahoney, Jari Arkko, and Roman Danyliw noted that these represent distinct stages or concepts in the process rather than interchangeable synonyms.
  - **RFC 1311 (STD Notes - Issue #83):** Discussed incorporating or obsoleting RFC 1311. Rich Salz will review the ~50 remaining lines of relevant content and propose text or obsolete RFC 1311 in draft-ietf-procon-2026bis.
  - **Discuss Positions:** Proposals to mandate verifiable technical discussion for discuss positions will be placed on hold rather than closed, keeping them captured for potential future recharters (supported by Jean Mahoney and John Klensin; David Schinazi had suggested closing).

### draft-ietf-procon-2418bis
David Schinazi presented progress using the [2418bis](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-procon-2418bis-01) slide deck.
- **Working Group Roles:** Discussed listing example roles (e.g., Technical Advisors) in the text. Lars Eggert, Robert Sparks, Paul Wouters, Jean Mahoney, Andrew Campling, and John Klensin discussed the utility of these roles. The consensus was to maintain the current text listing example roles that exist or have existed in practice without adding rigid new definitions or removing them.
- **Document Adoption Text:** Paul Wouters, Sean Turner, Leslie Daigle, Barry Leiba, Roman Danyliw, John Klensin, Andrew Campling, and Jay Daley discussed text regarding how working group documents reflect consensus. Text will be updated to say editors/authors are tasked with "reflecting" or "incorporating the spirit of deliberations" into working group documents, acknowledging both authors and editors, and recognizing that intermediate drafts reflect ongoing discussions rather than final consensus.
- **Milestones:** Streamlined text proposed by Lars Eggert regarding working group milestone usage and management was accepted.
- **RFC 7221 Alignment:** Discussed whether to update or obsolete RFC 7221. Following input from Barry Leiba, Robert Sparks, Jari Arkko, Roman Danyliw, Andrew Campling, and Colin Perkins, the consensus was to leave RFC 7221 as-is without adding metadata updates, leaving open the possibility for a separate future document if needed.
- **Section 3.3 (Consultants):** Agreed to remove introductory sentences asserting that unfamiliarity with IETF process leads to poor technical design (supported by Jari Arkko, Roman Danyliw, and Andrew Campling).
- **Section 3.5 (Minutes & Proceedings):** Addressed outdated requirements (printable ASCII format, emailing minutes@ietf.org, including scanned blue sheets directly inside minutes). Following discussion with John Klensin, Roman Danyliw, Leslie Daigle, Lars Eggert, Barry Leiba, Colin Perkins, Steve Traugott, and Pete Resnick, the text will state that the meeting proceedings package includes minutes, agenda, and attendee lists, and that chairs are responsible for ensuring accurate session minutes are recorded and submitted.

### draft-ietf-procon-chair-delegate
Lars Eggert presented [draft-ietf-procon-chair-delegate-00](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-procon-draft-ietf-procon-chair-delegate-00-00).
- The draft allows the IETF Chair to delegate specific tasks and functions to other Area Directors (with their agreement) while the Chair retains ultimate accountability.
- Discussed the relationship between the IETF Chair role and the General Area AD (GenAD) role. John Klensin, David Schinazi, Jari Arkko, Roman Danyliw, Barry Leiba, and Mirja Kühlewind discussed whether GenAD duties can be load-balanced like other AD duties vs. decoupling the GenAD and IETF Chair positions via NomCom job descriptions.
- Lars Eggert noted that normal AD task delegation and load balancing are already permitted under current practices, and he will adjust the text accordingly based on list feedback.

### draft-ietf-procon-chair-standin
Lars Eggert presented [draft-ietf-procon-chair-standin-00](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-procon-draft-ietf-procon-chair-standin-00-00).
- **Terminology:** Replaced the term "stand-in" in the draft text with "acting IETF Chair".
- **Selection Mechanics:** Outlined procedures for when the IETF Chair is indisposed or the position becomes vacant. In such cases, the IESG selects an acting IETF Chair from willing ADs.
- **Edge Cases & Disagreements:** Discussed handling cases where a Chair is incapacitated (e.g., hospitalized) and unable to declare indisposition versus performance disputes. Roman Danyliw, Mirja Kühlewind, Leslie Daigle, Pete Resnick, and John Klensin agreed that performance disputes or refusal to step down belong in the formal recall process, whereas unexpected incapacity where the Chair cannot make a declaration allows the IESG to step in and appoint an acting Chair.

## Decisions and Action Items

1. **draft-ietf-procon-2026bis:**
   - **Decision:** Do not close "verifiable technical discussion for discuss positions" issues; keep them open on hold for potential future recharter.
   - **Action Item:** Rich Salz to publish draft-13 resolving draft archival text, terminology alignment, and RFC 1311 disposition, with the goal of submitting draft-ietf-procon-2026bis to the IESG by the end of the year.

2. **draft-ietf-procon-2418bis:**
   - **Decision:** Retain the example WG roles list without adding new definitions.
   - **Decision:** Do not update or mark RFC 7221 in metadata; leave it unchanged.
   - **Decision:** Remove outdated sentences in Section 3.3 regarding process history and technical design.
   - **Decision:** Update Section 3.5 to specify that proceedings include minutes, agendas, and attendee lists, with chairs held responsible for ensuring accuracy.
   - **Action Item:** David Schinazi to update draft-ietf-procon-2418bis with the agreed adoption, roles, section 3.3, and proceedings text.

3. **draft-ietf-procon-chair-delegate & draft-ietf-procon-chair-standin:**
   - **Decision:** Adopt the term "acting IETF Chair" in draft-ietf-procon-chair-standin.
   - **Decision:** Keep performance disputes under the recall process, while allowing IESG selection of an acting Chair during temporary incapacity or vacancy.
   - **Action Item:** Lars Eggert to incorporate feedback into updated revisions of both draft-ietf-procon-chair-delegate and draft-ietf-procon-chair-standin.

## Next Steps

- Following the publication of revised drafts for draft-ietf-procon-2026bis and draft-ietf-procon-2418bis, the chairs will issue a joint Working Group Last Call (WGLC) for both documents.
- Robert Sparks volunteered as a dedicated document reviewer for draft-ietf-procon-2418bis prior to/during WGLC.
- Discussions on draft-ietf-procon-chair-delegate and draft-ietf-procon-chair-standin will continue on the PROCON mailing list once updated revisions are published.